From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mostly_Harmless <geek520170@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:30:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(list): free the user, gift and special parts of each
 danmaku

freeList() released only the text and the node, so every danmaku read
with user=, gift/sc/guard or as a mode 7 special danmaku from XML leaked
its separately allocated parts. mergeGiftDanmaku() already frees these
parts, so they are owned by their node.

readJson(), readAss() and readTemplateFile() left the pointers
uninitialised. readJson() keeps unknown types as they are, so a JSON
danmaku with type 5 became a SPECIAL danmaku whose special pointer was
garbage when writeAss() dereferenced it. Initialise the pointers to
NULL so freeList() can release them for every reader.
---
 src/AssFile/AssFile.c         | 2 ++
 src/List/DanmakuFactoryList.c | 3 +++
 src/XmlFile.c                 | 1 -
 3 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/AssFile/AssFile.c b/src/AssFile/AssFile.c
index dc2c7c5..4aa3753 100644
--- a/src/AssFile/AssFile.c
+++ b/src/AssFile/AssFile.c
@@ -849,6 +849,8 @@ int assFileToDanmaku(ASSFILE *inputSub, DANMAKU **danmakuHead, const char *mode,
                 return 5;
             }
             newDanmakuNode->special = NULL;
+            newDanmakuNode->user = NULL;
+            newDanmakuNode->gift = NULL;
 
             /*
              *+-------------+---------+
diff --git a/src/List/DanmakuFactoryList.c b/src/List/DanmakuFactoryList.c
index 144a94d..be938c3 100644
--- a/src/List/DanmakuFactoryList.c
+++ b/src/List/DanmakuFactoryList.c
@@ -415,6 +415,9 @@ void freeList(DANMAKU *listHead)
     {
         listHead = ptr->next;
         free(ptr->text); /* 释放文本部分的空间 */
+        free(ptr->user);
+        free(ptr->gift);
+        free(ptr->special);
         free(ptr);
         ptr = listHead;
     }
diff --git a/src/XmlFile.c b/src/XmlFile.c
index 24dd4a0..2f8317e 100644
--- a/src/XmlFile.c
+++ b/src/XmlFile.c
@@ -838,7 +838,6 @@ static void errorExit(FILE *ipF, DANMAKU *head, DANMAKU *ptr)
     if (head != NULL)
     {
         ptr->next = NULL;
-        ptr->special = NULL;
         freeList(head);
     }
     return;
